WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.260
- I know that many of you

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:03.300
would love to become more productive.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.910
And this certainly applies to me as well.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:08.190
But how can you accomplish that?

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:10.680
One person from the audience
a couple of weeks ago

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.560
sent me a list from a
service called Filtered

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.070
where they analyzed about
100 productivity hacks

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.360
and made a ranking out of it.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:21.300
So welcome to a new coffee
break here on my channel.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.230
In this video,

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:25.050
I will look into the top
10 productivity hacks.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.280
And I will give you my view

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.620
whether these are really effective or not.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:29.453
In the past,

00:00:29.453 --> 00:00:30.540
I was sometimes a bit skeptical

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:31.890
about these productivity tips.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.110
I made a video about
this in the past as well,

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.120
linking it somewhere above here,

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.500
but in the end of this video,

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.140
I will also share one bonus tip,

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.080
productivity tip that
really helped me in my life.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:45.000
So stay tuned and get into it.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.160
The first productivity
tip I want to talk about

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.780
is time boxing.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:51.480
Time boxing means that
you look at your calendar,

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.730
you plan your week or your month ahead,

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:56.760
and you schedule some
time into your calendar

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.970
for things that you really
would like to accomplish.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:02.401
And I feel like this
is especially effective

00:01:02.401 --> 00:01:05.940
for things that are outside
of your regular work.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.260
Of course, in your regular work,

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:09.270
you know that you will
need to make the time

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.680
for the things that really matter.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.990
But what is everything
that comes on top of that?

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:16.050
Maybe you have some side projects
that you want to work on.

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.000
Maybe you have an exercise routine

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.560
that you want to prioritize.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.740
Make sure that you block off
this time in the calendar

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:23.970
and then be realistic.

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:25.560
Do you even have enough time

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.920
in the evenings, on the
weekends to get this done?

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.950
Make sure to prioritize
accordingly to get this right.

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.540
Next step is prioritization.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.370
It is of course essential that at work,

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:37.530
you prioritize your
tasks in the right way.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.910
So let me share three tips here.

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:40.410
These are rather rule of thumbs

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.450
that I think apply most of the time.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.010
First, focus on things

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.530
that need to move to other people's desks.

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:49.320
So if someone else is waiting
for an input from you,

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:52.080
then this person's able
to progress the work

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.180
by him or herself, prioritize this.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.970
Make sure you get this through
this other person's desk

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:58.170
as quickly as possible

00:01:58.170 --> 00:01:59.310
because then you can also expect

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:01.860
to get the result back rather quickly

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.690
while significantly
increasing productivity

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.620
of the whole team.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:08.070
Next, do things first that
lead to some quick wins,

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:09.690
to some quick results.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:12.660
It's often quite frustrating
if you receive a project,

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.670
a task, maybe from your leadership,

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.320
and you do some things first

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:17.153
where you know

00:02:17.153 --> 00:02:20.040
that only in one or two
or three days of work,

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.650
you can actually have something
presentable in your hand.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:23.483
And of course,

00:02:23.483 --> 00:02:25.980
then if your leadership reaches
out to you after one day,

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:27.180
ask what you have done

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.610
and you don't really have
anything you can show for,

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:30.780
that's often not ideal.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:32.460
And third, to prevent burnout,

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:35.130
especially when you're sitting
at your desk in the evening,

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:36.208
it's already getting late,

00:02:36.208 --> 00:02:40.200
always ask yourself this
specific piece of work

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:43.080
where you now feel like you
need to work on it right now,

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.720
do you really need it for tomorrow?

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:48.150
Is it needed for your workday tomorrow?

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:49.165
And if it's not,

00:02:49.165 --> 00:02:51.990
do not work on it in the evening.

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:53.970
Next is the skill of saying no,

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:55.560
especially juniors often feel

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.360
like they need to do everything

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.250
that someone asks them to do.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:01.650
This is of course not
really a sustainable way

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:02.880
of looking at your work.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.140
And if you struggle with this,

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:07.110
if you struggle with saying
no in such a work environment,

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:07.943
I created a video in the past

00:03:07.943 --> 00:03:10.800
where I also shared specific
tips on this situation.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:11.880
I will link it above here,

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:12.900
feel free to check it out.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:15.450
Next productivity tip is
to move during the day.

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:17.520
If you just sit in front of a big screen

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:20.280
from early morning until late evening,

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.250
you will very likely get
depressed at some point.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:26.610
Your energy level just
naturally will go down.

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:27.930
What I implemented for myself

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.700
is now since a couple of weeks,

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:33.240
almost every day from Monday
to Friday during lunch break,

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:34.890
I go to the gym.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:37.680
I signed up for a gym
very close to my office.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:39.990
And then often I just pick
up something quick to eat

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:41.850
during a video conference
or something like that

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:43.830
so that I do get some food in as well.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:46.500
I know this is not possible
in every single job,

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:49.020
but even at McKinsey during
my time in consulting

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:52.170
I was able to at least go for short walk,

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:54.150
maybe outside of your client's building,

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:55.770
outside of your home.

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:59.250
This does make a big difference
just to get some fresh air

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.200
because otherwise there might be days

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.970
where I don't even see the sun.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:03.870
If in the early morning,

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:04.860
you go into the office,

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:05.693
and then afterwards,

00:04:05.693 --> 00:04:06.810
you come back from the office,

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:08.430
the sun has already gone down,

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:11.520
that's of course not really
great environment to work in.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.500
Next step, control your devices.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.840
We all have experienced the situation,

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.370
you receive a new email

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:18.630
and then you open Slack

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:21.120
and you see five unread messages on Slack,

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:22.380
then you look at your phone,

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:24.750
lots of notifications on your phone.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:27.390
How can you even concentrate
in this environment?

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:30.570
How can you even get anything
done in this situation?

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:32.460
Try to schedule some
time in your calendar,

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:34.200
maybe with time boxing,

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.480
where you focus on working on your emails

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:38.910
to make sure that you
really have some time

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:40.270
of uninterrupted work

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:42.690
where you can do some deep work done

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.190
without getting interrupted all the time

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:45.210
by these types of things.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:47.490
If so far you took any
value out of this video,

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:49.050
please destroy the like button

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:51.300
and subscribe for the YouTube algorithm.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.100
This would be much appreciated.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:53.933
And of course,

00:04:53.933 --> 00:04:56.040
if you have additional tips
on productivity to share,

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:57.900
leave me a comment in the comment section.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:59.250
But now let's continue.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:01.710
Next productivity tip
is to take short breaks.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:04.800
This is of course very much
related to the tip to move.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:05.633
But of course,

00:05:05.633 --> 00:05:08.580
if you are the personality that
just sits at his or her desk

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:10.410
and you really struggle
to do something else,

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:11.970
think about other tasks,

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:14.550
incorporate a couple
of these short breaks.

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:15.990
Frankly, in an office environment,

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:18.360
often this would be just a
quick chat with a colleague

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.680
and then a coffee break.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:21.030
In my humble opinion,

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:22.680
most people in these environments

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:25.080
don't really like these types of breaks.

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:26.160
But if you do,

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:27.390
make sure to have the time.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:30.510
For me, again, a big game
changer was the exercise.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:32.310
The gym time during the day,

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:35.130
that in itself is of course
a valued break as well.

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:36.090
Next productivity hack

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:38.610
is to have an actively managed to do list,

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:40.140
either on a written sheet

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:42.720
or just one of the many
to do management apps

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:44.160
that you can get on your mobile phone,

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:46.230
on the PC, on Mac and so on.

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:48.150
The main reason why this makes sense

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:50.880
is because it gives you peace of mind.

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:53.370
If you don't write down all your to dos,

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.680
first, it's very likely that
you will forget something.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:57.840
And second, you will always feel stressed

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:01.050
because suddenly some to
dos pop up in your mind

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:02.160
and you don't really know

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:04.320
whether this is something
to do now or maybe later.

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:06.390
You are just afraid of forgetting it.

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:08.880
So whenever you get a new task
that you need to get done,

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:12.210
just dump it in any of these
to do management programs

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:14.160
because then you know for sure

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.050
that you will have them all written down,

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:17.970
that you won't forget anything.

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:18.803
And besides that,

00:06:18.803 --> 00:06:20.400
maybe that's also personality thing,

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.380
but I feel like there's very few things

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:23.693
which are as satisfying

00:06:23.693 --> 00:06:26.310
as having a sheet of
paper in front of you,

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:27.930
even also one of these apps,

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:32.040
and being able to just cross
off to dos from that list.

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.540
That personally always gives me

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:35.550
a little sense of
accomplishment during the day.

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:37.350
A little sense of self-efficacy.

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:40.080
So if you feel in a similar
way about that, try it out.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.600
Next productivity tip is to eat well.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:44.070
Trust, we've all had the experience

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.230
of having had a very heavy lunch

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:48.600
and then in the afternoon,
just feeling down.

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.880
Just feeling like you lack any energy

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:52.920
to get anything productive done

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:55.200
for the next one, two or even three hours.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:56.310
That's of course not great

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:58.230
and probably also not really healthy.

00:06:58.230 --> 00:06:59.520
So avoid heavy lunches,

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.830
and also be careful about all the snacks

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:03.390
that you eat during the day.

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:06.150
In some companies and
almost all meeting rooms,

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:09.420
there are baskets of sweets,
of chocolate and so on.

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:11.760
And just so easy to
every in other meeting,

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:13.560
eating a bit of this chocolate.

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:15.210
So try to replace these snacks

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:16.860
with more healthy alternatives.

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:19.530
Next productivity tip
is the two minute rule.

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:22.470
This rule says that whenever
you can get a task done

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:23.490
in two minutes,

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:24.600
do it now.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:26.400
Don't postpone it to later.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:28.650
If something can get done in two minutes,

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:32.310
there's really no reason to
not taking action right now.

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:35.880
Don't even bother tracking
it in your to do app.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:37.380
Just the fact that you've opened your app

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:39.930
or take your piece of
paper with your to dos

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:41.160
and you write it down,

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.440
this alone will take
one minute or so, right?

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:45.660
So just get it done right now,

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:47.280
then it's finished and you're fine.

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:50.790
Next step is to control your
social media consumption.

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:53.760
This is a problem that many
people have, me included,

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:57.270
that you just waste far too
much time on all these apps,

00:07:57.270 --> 00:08:00.390
Instagram, Facebook, TikTok and so on.

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:02.160
I think in most professional contexts,

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:03.690
it's actually LinkedIn.

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:06.434
LinkedIn now became
this big social network

00:08:06.434 --> 00:08:08.670
where you can read all these posts,

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.320
watch all these videos.

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:12.316
And the mean thing is that for many jobs,

00:08:12.316 --> 00:08:14.220
you actually need LinkedIn.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:16.680
It's one of the tools that
you need for your job.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:17.850
Frankly, due to this reason,

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:20.460
I haven't even found a good
way of organizing myself

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:21.420
in this regard.

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:23.520
So if you have any good
tips to share on that,

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:25.603
just leave a comment
in the comment section.

00:08:25.603 --> 00:08:28.869
Now, finally, I wanna
share the one bonus advice

00:08:28.869 --> 00:08:30.990
that was not even present in this list

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.190
that I initially talked about

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:35.310
but that I feel had a quite
significant impact on my life.

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:38.430
So many people are using
actually big headphones,

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:41.910
noise canceling headphones
in your work routine

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:43.920
to just blend out the noise and so on.

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.390
But in my humble experience,

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:48.090
there is something that
is far more effective

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:50.400
than all these noise canceling headphones,

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:52.350
and this is proper ear plugs.

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:54.840
Something like I have here in my hand.

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:57.540
I started using these in university,

00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:59.850
especially during exams.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:02.040
So it was always allowed during exams

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:04.500
to plug in earplugs like this.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:07.890
And I feel like just the fact
alone that I used ear plugs

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:09.630
during most of my exams

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:11.640
helped me to improve my grades

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:15.300
by at least one or two
points on all of these exams.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:16.410
At least for me personally,

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:18.300
this was such a game changer

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:20.910
in how well I was able to concentrate.

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:21.900
And even today,

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:25.440
whenever I want to have
focused quality work time

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:27.493
of one hour, two hours or so,

00:09:27.493 --> 00:09:31.020
I just wanna sit in front of
my desk to get something done,

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:35.400
there's nothing else that
helps me as much to concentrate

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:37.320
as proper earplugs.

